# MEM.LOG — latest corrections and reminders (working memory)

Read first each session; newest entries at the top. Stable lessons migrate to
`LEARNING.LOG`; volatile specifics stay in their referenced documents.

Entry format (2026-11-16 onward): one section per decision —
  ## <Topic>
  **User decision:** the owner's ruling, recorded as given
  **Agent suggestion:** what the agent proposed
  **Conclusion:** the effective rule going forward
  **Source:** CHG-#### / BLD-#### / LRN-#### cross-references
Pre-format bullet entries below the new sections are preserved history.

## Dissolve agents/skills/shared into agents/shared

**User decision:** `agents/skills/shared/**` is a sustantiate issue — move everything up into top-level `agents/shared/`, remove all emptied folders. Success = `agents/skills/shared` gone, files relocated successfully, paths updated.

**Agent suggestion:** `git mv` the four subtrees (contracts/host/providers/tools) wholesale; mechanical import-prefix rewrite over an explicit file list (historical docstrings excluded); re-pin boundary tests; add the old root to the retired-path guard; gate with ruff + full pytest before commit.

**Conclusion:** `agents/skills/shared/` removed. 28 modules now live under `agents/shared/{contracts,host,providers,tools}`; 46 reference replacements across 26 files; guard and AGENTS.md layout updated; gate green (ruff clean, pytest 180/180 twice).

**Source:** CHG-0005 · BLD-0002

## AGENTS.md layout records all folders

**User decision:** The File Locations layout in AGENTS.md must record **all** folders of the actual tree (no abbreviation like `<role>/`), and keep expanding as the build grows.

**Agent suggestion:** Verify the real tree first (directory inventory + content check of non-obvious folders), then write descriptions from evidence; mark empty leftovers explicitly.

**Conclusion:** Layout lists every folder with an evidence-based description. Six empty leftover test dirs (tests/{agent,builder,coder,fixtures,researcher,runtime}) are marked as removal candidates, pending user ruling.

**Source:** CHG-0003 · this session's tree inventory

## Records relocated to log/

**User decision:** All project records move into `log/`: INDEX.md, CHANGE.LOG, BUILT.LOG, LEARNING.LOG, MEM.LOG.

**Agent suggestion:** Move tracked logs with `git mv` (preserves rename detection), then update every reference in AGENTS.md and INDEX.md in the same delivery.

**Conclusion:** Records live under `log/`; AGENTS.md stays at root. References updated; history preserved through git renames.

**Source:** CHG-0004

## System host removal

**User decision:** `system/host/` will be removed; after removal, update the AGENTS.md folder structure too.

**Agent suggestion:** Verify before deleting: the directory held zero files and zero tracked content (empty shell + caches); its only references are retirement guards (`scripts/check_retired_paths.py`, `tests/quality/test_layering.py`) and one stale producer declaration (`agents/skills/planner/tools/gap_analysis.py`).

**Conclusion:** `system/host/` deleted from the tree. `system/` now contains only `scanner/` and `storage/`. AGENTS.md File Locations mirrors the real tree and must be expanded as the build grows.

**Source:** CHG-0003 · BLD-0001

## Storage Ownership

**User decision:** `system/storage/` owns persistence; `system/host/` owns orchestration.

**Agent suggestion:** Keep storage operations separate from workflow coordination.

**Conclusion:** Host delegates persistence to storage. No duplicated storage ownership.

**Source:** CHG-0002 · BLD-0001

## Removal finality

**User decision:** "when remove no need record or commit message."

**Agent suggestion:** Backup copies of removed files and commit-message proposals for removals.

**Conclusion:** File removals are final — no backup copies or recovery records, no commit-message proposals for removals. Delete, verify, move on. Backups only on explicit request.

**Source:** BLD-0001

